<article class="env-definition" id="0F3A">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0F3A">Definition <span data-tag="0F3A">37.75.2</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a locally quasi-finite morphism. A <em>weighting</em> or a <em>pondération</em> of $f$ is a map $w : X \to \mathbf{Z}$ such that for any diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ X \ar[d]_ f &  U \ar[l]^ h \ar[d]^\pi \\  Y &  V \ar[l]_ g }  \]
</div>
  <p> where $V \to Y$ is étale, $U \subset X_ V$ is open, and $U \to V$ finite, the function $\int _\pi (w \circ h)$ is locally constant. </p>
</article>